This is the first time I've encountered the Gnome With a Wand of Death
phenomenon, which is odd considering I have over a hundred characters
who have never descended past DL10 and by all rights in the myriad
ways I have found to die so far, I should have.

However, this time it was notable simply because I encountered the
abovementioned GWWD (in this case, G stands for goblin) on DL1. I was
an Arc, so no chance for MR or reflection at the start of the game,
and I had nothing other than starting equipment in my inventory yet. I
step into a room that appeared to be empty (I had fully explored
cleared this level already), and one step through the door, this
damned goblin zaps me with a /oLightning from flush against the wall
where there was no way I could have seen him. Absolutely no way to
avoid death.

I hate the RNG sometimes. I mean, it wasn't even my fault for leaving
a wand laying out on the floor or anything--I had looted the entire
level! I think Nethack just hates me.

Any other darkly amusing stories of immediate and unavoidable death
that recently occured to any of you?



